<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bitonto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1734</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bitonto was fought on 25 May 1734 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a>. A Spanish army under the Count of Montemar defeated the Austrian forces holding the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. The victory secured the kingdom for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-spain">Charles of Bourbon</a>, the future Charles III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and made Naples an independent monarchy under a Bourbon dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bitonto.jpg" alt="Battle of Bitonto" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Luigi Rocco · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Bitonto_by_Giovanni_Luigi_Rocco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
